{
  "animation": {
    "interpolate": true,
    "frametime": 1,
    "comment": "Scrolling belt surface. belt_top.png must be a VERTICAL strip of N square frames (e.g. 16x(16*N)) showing the tread translating one step per frame ALONG the belt length (the +Z / 'north->south' axis of the base model). Lower frametime = faster visual scroll. The scroll is a fixed client-side speed; it does NOT read RPM. Model y-rotation per `facing` rotates this face too, so the visible scroll always runs toward the belt's travel direction; up/down models tilt it along the ramp."
  }
}
